<title>USA: Turner Corp Q3 shr loss vs profit.</title>
<headline>Turner Corp Q3 shr loss vs profit.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>(in thousands except share amounts)</p>
<p>						    Three Months Ended</p>
<p>							  Sept. 30,</p>
<p>						  1996		  1995</p>
<p> New sales			     $  812,000	  $  783,000</p>
<p> Value of construction completed $  912,133	  $  889,978</p>
<p>Earnings from construction</p>
<p>  contracts				  21,201		19,019</p>
<p> Income from construction operations  2,253		 4,272</p>
<p> Net income (loss)			    375		 1,161</p>
<p>Net income (loss) per common share</p>
<p>						( 0.02)		  0.13</p>
<p>Weighted average number of shares</p>
<p>					    5,355,357	   5,305,340</p>
<p>						    Nine Months Ended</p>
<p>							 Sept. 30,</p>
<p>						    1996		1995</p>
<p> New sales				$2,700,000	 $2,200,000</p>
<p> Value of construction completed  $2,448,486	 $2,418,648</p>
<p>Earnings from construction</p>
<p>  contracts				   52,212	     53,591</p>
<p> Income from construction operations   4,874	     12,388</p>
<p> Net income (loss)			   ( 64)		3,318</p>
<p> Net income (loss) per common share  ( 0.27)		 0.37</p>
<p>Weighted average number of shares</p>
<p>					     5,335,015	  5,290,116</p>
<p>NOTE - Value of construction completed represents the cost of the work put in place and materials fabricated during the year and related earnings pursuant to Turner's construction and management contracts, together with fees and reimbursed expense from consulting contracts. The company said it is is essentially a measure of construction activity during the year rather than &quot;sales&quot; or &quot;revenues&quot; in the sense that the term is used in a typical manufacturing company.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610</p>
</text>
